cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HelioAI: a natural-language agent for heliophysics data discovery and analysis"
message: >-
  If HelioAI contributes to published work, please cite it. Please also cite the
  data providers you used (AMDA/CDPP, CDAWeb/NASA, CSA/ESA) and any scientific
  method references listed in the session's exported acknowledgements.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Furkan
    family-names: Erdogan
    email: furkan.erdogan.pro@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/erdoganfurkan/HelioAI"
url: "https://erdoganfurkan.github.io/HelioAI"
abstract: >-
  HelioAI is an AI agent for heliophysics and space plasma physics. It resolves
  natural-language descriptions to parameter identifiers across more than 70
  missions using hybrid semantic and lexical retrieval over the speasy catalogue,
  downloads the data, runs the analysis in a sandboxed Python environment, and
  exports the session as a self-contained, re-runnable Jupyter notebook. Derived
  quantities are computed from cited recipes so that every result carries its
  method and reference.
keywords:
  - heliophysics
  - space physics
  - plasma physics
  - solar wind
  - magnetosphere
  - reproducibility
  - large language models
  - AI agent
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-07-29"
